<Defs>

  <!--
    The Deepwell Union (docs/design/peoples-third.md, the second of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release F";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesF.cs): miners and drillers who struck it rich and lost it all when the seam ran
    dry, and stayed together anyway. The union's book holds every member and every shift; a strike is called by vote, never
    by one man. Industrial, on the game's outlander parent; they arise in every age (ariseAges 0~3), and rise toward the
    spacer age at a middling pace, digging for whatever the new age needs (agePace 11). No uniform: hard hats (Vanilla
    Apparel Expanded), work clothes varied by trade; their signature is the union's red, an armband (Biotech's sash, worn
    as one) over a red work shirt of any cut. Shovels (Vanilla Weapons Expanded's tools), shotguns (the game's, Vanilla
    Weapons Expanded's trench guns and sawn-offs) and the shot-firers' blasting charges (the game's grenades, Vanilla
    Factions Expanded - Settlers' dynamite where it is loaded). Tough, strong miners, and a few with mining genes (Biotech's
    dark vision and robust, Alpha Genes' high mining yield); A RimWorld of Magic's geomancers among them. Their towns are
    pits: a headframe over the shaft, a boarding house, a slag heap and the union hall (Rimfolk_Plan_UnionPit). At the
    gate: a drill crew offers to drill the colony's deep ground for a share of what comes up, a mining accident at the
    game's rate if the colony's hand works the drill with them (Rimfolk_Evt_UnionDrill); an assayer sells steel,
    components and blasting goods (Rimfolk_Evt_UnionGoods); in a strike their trade stalls (no caravans, no trade at their
    towns, none from their visitors) until the colony helps settle it at the gate (Rimfolk_Evt_UnionStrike). Their ask: two
    good miners for a short shift (Rimfolk_Mission_UnionShift). Their founding: Marta Grieve and the vote to stay. Faith
    (Ideology): the union as one (collectivist), the tunnellers, and Vanilla Ideology Expanded's industrialism. Kinds of
    people: dirtmoles, Neanderthals, wasters, the Stoneborn, boglegs, Korgs and awakened gorillas, four in five baseliners.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Deepwell</defName>
    <label>Deepwell Union</label>
    <description>A union of miners and drillers who go down into the ground for whatever it keeps, and come up covered in it. They drill for anyone who will pay a share, sell steel and blasting goods to anyone who will buy, and argue about all of it in the union hall. Every member and every shift is in the union's book, and a strike is called by vote, never by one man.\n\nTheir ways began in a boomtown that struck it rich and then lost it all. The seam under Deepwell ran dry in a single season, the owners left in the night, and the shift-captain Marta Grieve called the miners into the hall and put it to a vote: scatter, or stay together and dig somewhere else. They voted to stay, wrote every name in a book, and walked out with their picks the next morning. That book is still read at every meeting, and every member still ties on the union's red armband before going down.\n\nThey are loud, blunt and loyal, quick to laugh and quick to vote. They hate a cave-in, a boss who decides alone and a silent pit. Each pit is run by its shift-captain, and the union by its union boss, elected every year.</description>
    <pawnSingular>union miner</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>union miners</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>union boss</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Deepwell_Miner</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Deepwell</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_DeepwellTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Deepwell</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/DeepwellTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
